---
import LegalPage from "@/components/LegalPage.astro";
import { site } from "@/data/site";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy policy | ${site.name}`}
  lang="en"
  alternateHref="/de/datenschutz"
>
  <LegalPage title="Privacy policy">
    <p>
      This is a translation. The{" "}
      <a href="/de/datenschutz" hreflang="de">
        German version
      </a>{" "}
      is legally binding.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <address>
      {site.name}
      <br />
      {site.country.en}
    </address>
    <p>
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>

    <h2>2. Hosting via Cloudflare</h2>
    <p>
      This website is provided via Cloudflare Pages, a service of Cloudflare,
      Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. All requests to this
      website pass through Cloudflare's global server network. In the process,
      Cloudflare processes technically necessary data, in particular your IP
      address, the requested address, date and time, your browser type and the
      previously visited page (referrer). This data is needed to deliver the
      site and to protect it against attacks and abuse, for example through
      filter rules against automated access.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare stores this data in server log files for a limited period and
      uses it to create aggregated statistics, for example on the number of
      visits or the countries of origin. These statistics do not allow any
      conclusions to be drawn about individual persons.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. My legitimate interest is the
      secure, fast and reliable provision of this website. Data may be
      transferred to the USA. Cloudflare is certified under the EU-US Data
      Privacy Framework, which ensures an adequate level of data protection.
    </p>
    <p>
      For more information, see{" "}
      <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Cloudflare's privacy policy
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>3. Audience measurement with Cloudflare Web Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      To understand how many people visit this website and how fast it loads, I
      use Cloudflare Web Analytics, a service of Cloudflare, Inc. (see section
      2). When you open a page, a small script from Cloudflare is loaded. It
      sends the requested page, the previously visited page (referrer), your
      browser, operating system and device type, and page load measurements to
      Cloudflare. Your country is derived from your IP address. According to
      Cloudflare, IP addresses and browser data are not used to recognise
      individual visitors.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare Web Analytics does not set cookies, does not store any
      information in your browser and does not create user profiles. I only see
      aggregated statistics, for example the number of page views per day, and
      cannot draw any conclusions about individual persons from them.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. My legitimate interest is to
      understand the reach of my portfolio and to distinguish real visits from
      automated access. You can prevent the measurement by blocking scripts from
      static.cloudflareinsights.com in your browser, for example with a content
      blocker. Section 2 applies accordingly to transfers to the USA.
    </p>

    <h2>4. No cookies, no profiles</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not set cookies and does not use any advertising or
      tracking services that follow your behaviour across websites or create
      profiles. Fonts are loaded locally from this website, so no connections to
      third parties are made for them. Connections to third parties are only
      made through hosting and audience measurement (sections 2 and 3) and if
      you use the contact form (section 6) or the chat assistant (section 7).
    </p>

    <h2>5. Contact by email</h2>
    <p>
      If you send me an email, I process your information solely to handle your
      request. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR if your request relates to a
      contract or pre-contractual measures, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. Your
      data is deleted as soon as it is no longer needed for this purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Contact form</h2>
    <p>
      If you use the contact form, your name, email address and message are
      transmitted so that your request can be delivered to me by email. The
      legal basis and deletion are handled as described in section 5.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Spam protection:</strong> To protect against spam and abuse, I use
      Cloudflare Turnstile, a service of Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San
      Francisco, CA 94107, USA. Turnstile is only loaded once you interact with
      the form. Cloudflare processes technical data such as your IP address and
      browser information to check whether the request comes from a human. The
      legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. My legitimate interest is protecting the
      form against automated abuse.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Processing and delivery:</strong> The form data is sent to a
      function I operate on Cloudflare (Cloudflare Workers). It checks the
      request and passes it to Resend, an email service of Resend, Inc., USA,
      for delivery. Cloudflare logs technical request data, such as the IP
      address, for a limited time for troubleshooting and security. Resend
      stores the sent email according to its retention periods.
    </p>
    <p>
      Both providers may transfer data to the USA. For more information, see the{" "}
      <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Cloudflare privacy policy
      </a>{" "}
      and the{" "}
      <a
        href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Resend privacy policy
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>7. Chat assistant</h2>
    <p>
      On this website you can ask an AI-powered chat assistant questions about
      my professional background. The assistant only becomes active when you
      open the chat window and send a message.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Spam protection:</strong> When you send your first message,
      Cloudflare Turnstile is loaded to prevent automated abuse. The information
      on Turnstile in section 6 applies accordingly.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Processing of your messages:</strong> Your message and the
      previous messages of the current conversation (at most ten) are sent to a
      function I operate on Cloudflare (Cloudflare Workers). Using Cloudflare
      Workers AI and Cloudflare Vectorize, it searches my own knowledge base for
      relevant information and passes your question, the conversation and this
      information to the language model Claude provided by Anthropic Ireland,
      Limited, Ireland. Claude generates an answer, which is sent straight back
      to your browser. Processing may take place in the USA, safeguarded by
      Anthropic's data processing agreement. Under its terms, Anthropic may not
      use the content to train its models and only keeps it for a limited period
      according to its retention periods.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Storage:</strong> I do not store your conversations. The
      conversation only exists in your open browser tab and is gone once you
      reload the page, close the tab or reset the conversation. To limit abuse
      and costs, your browser receives a random session identifier that is valid
      for 30 minutes and does not allow any conclusions about you. Only
      technical information such as the number of processed text units is
      logged, not the content of your messages. Cloudflare logs technical
      request data, such as the IP address, for a limited time. If you resize
      the chat window, this setting is stored locally in your browser. It never
      leaves your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please do not enter sensitive personal data in the chat. The answers are
      generated automatically and may be inaccurate. Only information I give you
      personally is binding.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. My legitimate interest is to offer
      visitors an easy way to learn about my background and to protect the
      service against abuse. For more information, see{" "}
      <a
        href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Anthropic's privacy policy
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>8. Links to other websites</h2>
    <p>
      This website contains links to GitHub and LinkedIn. Data is only
      transferred to these providers once you click one of these links. Their
      own privacy policies apply there.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR you have the right at any time to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access the data stored about you (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
      <li>have inaccurate data rectified (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
      <li>have your data erased (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
      <li>restrict the processing of your data (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
      <li>receive your data in a portable format (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
      <li>object to the processing (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
      <li>lodge a complaint with a data protection authority (Art. 77 GDPR)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To do so, simply contact me by email at{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <p>Last updated: November 2026</p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
